lake|PASS: Inland water surrounded by land matches the literal noun without restricting all lakes to fresh water. The route and old mill are fictional; in/by/around constructions and capitalization guidance are qualified.
risky|PASS: A possible adverse outcome is distinguished from certainty of harm. The stopped-delivery example grounds business risk without advice; riskier/riskiest and the Vietnamese causal timing are accurate.
surrounding|PASS: Relative nearby position is explained without inventing an absolute distance. The market serves both town and villages; normally attributive guidance distinguishes the adjective from an independent place noun.
wealth|PASS: Financial riches and figurative abundance retain separate source ordinals. A wealth of information is not assigned countable-money status; trading-business origin and archive examples translate faithfully.
determined|PASS: Firm intention is separated from a passive determination of a date. Mastering rhythm illustrates purposeful persistence; determined to and determined effort provide reusable construction guidance.
